{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba \\\"/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/CURRENT_STATE.md\\\" | sed -n '1642,1669p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1642\t## Part 30 — Offline-download bug fixed: formal-track downloads were caching the wrong audio path\n  1643\t\n  1644\t**The bug**: `getAudioUrlsForModule()` in `app/app.js` still resolved every non-vocational (formal) module\n  1645\tto its single legacy `module.audioFile` path (e.g. `audio/n1-maths-01.mp3`). But the segmented player added\n  1646\tin Part 27 plays and caches audio keyed by each segment's own `audioFile`\n  1647\t(`audio/n1-maths-01-01/-02/-03.mp3`, from `module.segments[]`, added in Part 26). Effect: the \"download for\n  1648\toffline\" flow was fetching/caching a URL the player never looks up, so offline formal-track audio silently\n  1649\tdid nothing useful — and once real segmented recordings replace the legacy bare files, that stale path\n  1650\twon't even exist to download.\n  1651\t\n  1652\t**Fix**: `getAudioUrlsForModule()` now returns `module.segments[].audioFile` (3 URLs) for any formal module\n  1653\tthat has segments, falling back to the legacy single `audioFile` only if a module somehow lacks `segments`\n  1654\t(none currently do — all 359 formal modules have them per Part 26). `getAudioEntriesForGradeBand()`'s\n  1655\tper-item `moduleId` labelling was also fixed: it previously suffixed only vocational multi-lesson entries\n  1656\twith `-01/-02/...`; now it suffixes any module yielding more than one URL, so the 3 formal segments per\n  1657\tmodule get distinct labels instead of 3 identical `moduleId`s. Everything downstream (download items,\n  1658\t`readyForOffline`, `missingCount`, cache-cleanup on module completion) already operated per-URL/per-item,\n  1659\tnot per-module, so no other changes were needed.\n  1660\t\n  1661\t**Verification**: `node -c app/app.js` (syntax)