{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"The core fix is correct for the current validated corpus, but I found a cleanup gap the prior account did not mention: cache cleanup now targets the three segment keys, yet it no longer targets legacy `audio/<moduleId>.mp3` rows created by the old buggy downloader. Those stale rows can remain in IndexedDB; additionally, per-key deletion errors are swallowed, so the cleanup can report success while a row survives. I’ll distinguish these from the core download/playback key-space fix in the report."}}
